    "body": "@mkinney - Maintainer's decision (question dialog, 2026-11-12) on the case the review of PR #1265 found still open - a turning operation on a MILL-TURN posted through a milling post: **\"Refuse it\"**. Rule: a section that turns the work (a turning op or an on-centre drill, as `lathe_voice::voice_of` reads it) is posted only through a turning post; through a milling post it is refused by name, on a mill-turn as on a lathe. Milling and C-axis sections through a milling post on a mill-turn still post. The shipped Mill-turn machine's default post stays as it is. The existing pin `lathe_workholding_mill_post` (\"posts at the chuck limit\") becomes a refusal test - stricter, not looser.\n\nSo blocker 1 of the review above is to be fixed in this PR (one derivation: refuse a work-spindle section when the post's `work_voice` is not turning), together with blocker 2 (the PR body is another PR's and would close #1247 - please replace it, with a `Changelog:` line and the closing keyword for #1232 only) and blocker 3 (keep the plain lathe for the three generate-only tests in `lathe_cross_drill.rs`). Main is frozen at `0757563d` while conflicts are cleared; this fix is wanted as soon as it is clean.",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
